<svg class="diagram-svg" viewBox="0 0 560 365" role="img" aria-labelledby="bdl07laplacecontours-title bdl07laplacecontours-desc" data-pagefind-ignore>
  <title id="bdl07laplacecontours-title">Laplace approximation on a two-parameter network</title>
  <desc id="bdl07laplacecontours-desc">Grey contour lines of the energy over the two parameters theta 1 and theta 2, each from minus 3 to 3. The landscape has two symmetric minima, one near theta 1 equal to 1.6 and theta 2 equal to 1, the other near minus 1.6 and minus 1, separated by a ridge through the origin. A dot marks the right-hand minimum theta star; a thick solid ellipse around it shows one standard deviation and a thick dashed ellipse two standard deviations of the Laplace approximation. The ellipses follow the local curvature at the minimum but extend over regions where the true energy rises steeply and miss the second minimum entirely.</desc>
